@prefix : <https://github.com/kataph/function-method-ontology#> .
@prefix dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix DOLCE: <http://www.loa.istc.cnr.it/dolce/dolce-owl/DOLCE#> .
@prefix terms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix iof-av: <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/> .
@base <https://github.com/kataph/function-method-ontology#> .

<https://w3id.org/fumco> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                          owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/fumco/1.1> ;
                          owl:imports <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic/3.5> ;
                          terms:abstract """FUMCO: FUnctions, Methods, and Capabilities Ontology

Attachment to the paper \"About functions, behaviours, and capabilities in formal ontology and engineering\" in submission to the Semantic Web Journal, this ontology exemplify how the first order theory described in the paper can be translated in OWL (https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/full/10.3233/SW-223188, see also the relevant GitHub repository: https://www.github.com/kataph/FUMCO).

The Dolce-owl ontology used is the current version of DOLCEbasic exposed at the address http://www.w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic (and stored in the repository https://github.com/appliedontolab/DOLCE/tree/main/OWL)"""@en ;
                          terms:contributor "Francesco Compagno" ;
                          terms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
                          terms:title "FUMCO: FUnctions, Methods, and Capabilities Ontology" ;
                          rdfs:label "FUMCO: FUnctions, Methods, and Capabilities Ontology" ;
                          owl:versionInfo """1.1.0

- removed erroneous axiom (Connect disjointed with its own superclass)
- updated the DOLCE-OWL import to current version of DOLCE-basic
- retconnetted the name of the ontology to FUMCO (FUnctions, Methods, and Capabilities Ontology)
- changed the last separator in the root IRI from \"#\" to \"/\"
- the ontology is now exposed at the address https://w3id.org/fumco 
- the ontology IRI is now https://w3id.org/fumco
- restructured and enriched the annotations of the ontology
- splitted the ontology from the examplificative Abox (which is now present in a different file in the repository).""" .

#################################################################
#    Annotation properties
#################################################################

###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract
terms:abstract rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/license
terms:license rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/title
terms:title rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example
skos:example rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/firstOrderLogicAxiom
iof-av:firstOrderLogicAxiom rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/firstOrderLogicDefinition
iof-av:firstOrderLogicDefinition rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive
iof-av:isPrimitive rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition
iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale
iof-av:primitiveRationale rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom
iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/semiFormalNaturalLanguageDefinition
iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageDefinition rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


#################################################################
#    Datatypes
#################################################################

###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/ohms
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/ohms> rdf:type rdfs:Datatype .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/volts
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/volts> rdf:type rdfs:Datatype .


#################################################################
#    Object Properties
#################################################################

###  https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#constantPartOf
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#constantPartOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ,
                                                                owl:TransitiveProperty ;
                                                       rdfs:domain <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#Endurant> ;
                                                       rdfs:range <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#Endurant> .


###  https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#constantQualeOf
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#constantQualeOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                        rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty .


###  https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#directQualityOf
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#directQualityOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                        rdfs:domain <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#Quality> .


###  https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#specificallyDependsOn
<https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#specificallyDependsOn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                              rdfs:comment """Specific dependance can be understood in modal terms. It can also be understood in temporal only terms, e.g.:

specificallyDependsOn(x,y) ⇐⇒(∃t(PRE(x,t)) ∧∀t(PRE(x,t) =⇒PRE(y,t)))

The above notion of dependence is specific and existential: x depends on y if and only if x exists at some time and at any time when x exists so does y."""@en .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/causally-contributes-to
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/causally-contributes-to> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                     rdfs:domain <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#Perdurant> ;
                                                     rdfs:range <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#Perdurant> ;
                                                     rdfs:isDefinedBy "This relation abstracts causal explanations of complex occurences.  For example, \"the beam was cut, therefore it fell to the floor\": we could introduce in the domain of discourse two perdurants: \"cutting the beam [in some context]\" and \"falling to the floor [in some context]\" and then state causally-contributes-to(\"cutting the beam\", \"falling to the floor\")" ;
                                                     rdfs:label "causally contributes to" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/classified-by
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/classified-by> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                                           owl:inverseOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/classifies> ;
                                           rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Concept> ;
                                           rdfs:isDefinedBy "https://www.istc.cnr.it/en/content/social-roles-and-their-descriptions" ;
                                           rdfs:label "classified by" ;
                                           iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "The relation between a reified concept and any of its instances" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/classifies
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/classifies> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Concept> ;
                                        rdfs:label "classifies" ;
                                        iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "inferse of classified by" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/definition-founded-on
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/definition-founded-on> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                                                   rdfs:label "definition founded on" ;
                                                   iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "x is definition-founded on some entity y if and only if y is necessarily used to define x." .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/external-to
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/external-to> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:comment "This relation expresses the fact that two entities are 'external'. The precise definition of the external-to relation depends on the underlying reference ontology. Using DOLCE we defined it as follows: x is external to y if and only if x is neither a quality of y, nor one of y’s constituents, nor x and y have parts in common." ;
                                         rdfs:label "external to" ;
                                         iof-av:firstOrderLogicDefinition "externalTo(x,y) ↔ ¬(qt(x,y) ∨constitutes(x,y) ∨O(x,y))" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/follows
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/follows> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                     rdfs:comment """follows is defined differently depending on its relata:

in the case the relata are perdurants

df31 follows(x, y) =df precedes(y, x)

In the case the relata are types
df33 follows(Φ, Ψ) =df ∀x(Ψ(x) =⇒ ∃y(Φ(y) ∧ follows(y, x)))
“Φ follows Ψ if for every instance of Ψ there is an instance of Φ that follows
it.”

In the case the relata are reified concepts:
df35 follows(c, d) =df ∀x(CL(x, d) =⇒ ∃y(CL(y, c) ∧ follows(y, x)))""" ;
                                     rdfs:label "follows" ;
                                     iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "if x and y are events, x follows y if its temporal extension is after (e.f. in the sense of Allen's) that of y. If x and y are at the type-level this definition is lifted appropriately." .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/function-of
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/function-of> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         owl:inverseOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/has-function> ;
                                         rdfs:domain <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/SelectedFunction> ;
                                         rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/TechnicalArtifact> ;
                                         rdfs:label "function of" ;
                                         iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "The relation between a function and the object such a function is attributed to by an agent's selection" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/has-function
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/has-function> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                          rdfs:domain <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/TechnicalArtifact> ;
                                          rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Concept> ;
                                          rdfs:label "has function" ;
                                          iof-av:firstOrderLogicDefinition """hasFunction(x, f) ↔ ∃a, qintentionalSel(a, e, x, q) ∧ defFoundedOn(q, f)
 ∧ Capability(q) ∧ qt(q, x)""" ;
                                          iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "The relation between an object and the function attributed to it by an agent's selection" ;
                                          iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageDefinition """“An entity has/bears/carries/has ascribed a function iff there is some agent (a)
that intentionally selects (though event e) a capability (q) of that entity that
makes the entity able of executing the function.”""" .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/has-function> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty iof-av:firstOrderLogicDefinition ;
   owl:annotatedTarget """hasFunction(x, f) ↔ ∃a, qintentionalSel(a, e, x, q) ∧ defFoundedOn(q, f)
 ∧ Capability(q) ∧ qt(q, x)""" ;
   rdfs:comment "The link between the capability and the function with the definition-founding relation, as was done before. Notice that f may be an ontological function, but also some more specific class, such as a systemic function."
 ] .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/has-main-function
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/has-main-function> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                               owl:inverseOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/main-function-of> ;
                                               rdfs:label "has main function" ;
                                               iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "The main function addressed by an engineering method, that is, the function such that a plan to execut it is detailed by the methos" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/has-systemic-function
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/has-systemic-function> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                   owl:inverseOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/systemic-function-of> ;
                                                   rdfs:domain <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/TechnicalArtifact> ;
                                                   rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/SystemicFunction> ;
                                                   rdfs:label "has systemic function" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/instantiation-founded-on
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/instantiation-founded-on> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                      rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                                                      rdfs:domain <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Concept> ;
                                                      rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Concept> ;
                                                      rdfs:comment """foundedInst(x, y) ⇐⇒ (CN(x)∧∃z, t(CL(z, x, t))∧∀z, t(CL(z, x, t) =⇒ ∃w(founded(z,w)∧CL(w, y, t))))
“the concept x is instantiation-founded on the concept y if and only if, given any z that plays x, then z is
founded on some instance of y”""" ;
                                                      rdfs:label "instantiation founded on" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/main-function-of
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/main-function-of> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                              rdfs:domain <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/SystemicFunction> ;
                                              rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/EngineeringMethod> ;
                                              rdfs:label "main function of" ;
                                              iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "inverse of has main function" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/partecipated-by-doer
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/partecipated-by-doer> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                  owl:inverseOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/participates-as-doer> ;
                                                  rdfs:domain <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Behaviour> ;
                                                  rdfs:range [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                               owl:unionOf ( <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#AgentiveSocialObject>
                                                                             <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/TechnicalArtifact>
                                                                           )
                                                             ] ;
                                                  rdfs:label "partecipated by doer" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/participates-as-doer
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/participates-as-doer> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/participates-in> ;
                                                  rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                owl:unionOf ( <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#AgentiveSocialObject>
                                                                              <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/TechnicalArtifact>
                                                                            )
                                                              ] ;
                                                  rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Behaviour> ;
                                                  rdfs:comment """This is a processual role contextualized by a behavior. For example, a cutting action entails that there is something that is the subject of the action, say a saw (or the system formed by a person or machine using the saw), and the object of the action, say a beam of wood. The same holds for pumping, joining, and other behaviors that can be described by transitive verbs.
The action subjects participate-as-doer to the behavior.""" ;
                                                  rdfs:label "participates as doer" ;
                                                  iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "The participation relation specialized to doers" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/participates-as-flow
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/participates-as-flow> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/participates-in> ;
                                                  rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Behaviour> ;
                                                  rdfs:comment """This is a processual role contextualized by a behavior. For example, a cutting action entails that there is something that is the subject of the action, say a saw (or the system formed by a person or machine using the saw), and the object of the action, say a beam of wood. The same holds for pumping, joining, and other behaviors that can be described by transitive verbs.
The action objects participate-as-flow to the behavior.

We do not add a Flow class to this ontology, leaving the issue to further research, or to domain-level extensions of this ontology.""" ;
                                                  rdfs:label "participates as flow" ;
                                                  iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "The participation relation specialized to flows" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/participates-in
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/participates-in> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topObjectProperty ;
                                             rdfs:domain <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#Endurant> ;
                                             rdfs:range <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#Perdurant> ;
                                             rdfs:label "participates in" ;
                                             iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "participation of an object in an occurrence. Originally a ternary relation in DOLCE containing the time of participation, here is de-temporalized by stipulating that \"x participates in y\" means \"x participates in y at at least some time t\"" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/plays-as
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/plays-as> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                      rdfs:subPropertyOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/classified-by> ;
                                      rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Role> ;
                                      rdfs:isDefinedBy "https://www.istc.cnr.it/en/content/social-roles-and-their-descriptions" ;
                                      rdfs:label "play as" ;
                                      iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "Specialization of the classification relation to the case of roles" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/precedes
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/precedes> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                      rdfs:comment "precedes" ,
                                                   """precedes is defined differently depending on its relata:

in the case the relata are perdurants
df30 precedes(x, y) =df ∃t, t′(ql(t, x)T ∧ ql(t′, y)T ∧ t ≤ t′)
“x precedes y if the time extension of x precedes that of y.”

In the case the relata are types
df32 precedes(Φ, Ψ) =df ∀x(Ψ(x) =⇒ ∃y(Φ(y) ∧ precedes(y, x)))
“Φ precedes Ψ if for every instance of Ψ there is an instance of Φ that
precedes it.”

In the case the relata are reified concepts:
df34 precedes(c, d) =df ∀x(CL(x, d) =⇒ ∃y(CL(y, c) ∧ precedes(y, x)))""" ;
                                      iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "As the \"follows\" relation, but with the temporal order exchanged" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/sub-concept-of
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/sub-concept-of> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            owl:inverseOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/super-concept-of> ;
                                            rdfs:domain <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Concept> ;
                                            rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Concept> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "subConceptOf(x, y)  ↔ (CN(x) ∧ CN(y) ∧ ∃z, t(CL(z, x, t)) ∧ ∀z, t(CL(z, x, t) → CL(z, y, t)))" ;
                                            rdfs:label "sub concept of" ;
                                            iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "Specialization relation between DOLCE concepts" ;
                                            iof-av:semiFormalNaturalLanguageDefinition "“A concept x is a sub-concept of a concept y if and only if all instances of x are also instances of y”" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/sub-function-of
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/sub-function-of> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                             rdfs:domain <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/SystemicFunction> ;
                                             rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/EngineeringMethod> ;
                                             rdfs:label "sub function of" ;
                                             iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "The relation linking a decomposing function to an engineering method: a function is the sub-function of an engineering method if it is required to be executed in order to execute a step of the engineerign method." .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/super-concept-of
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/super-concept-of> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                              rdfs:domain <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Concept> ;
                                              rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/Concept> ;
                                              rdfs:label "super concept of" ;
                                              iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "Inverse of sub concept of" .


###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/systemic-function-of
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/systemic-function-of> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                  rdfs:domain <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/SystemicFunction> ;
                                                  rdfs:range <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/TechnicalArtifact> ;
                                                  rdfs:label "systemic function of" ;
                                                  iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "The relation between a systemic function and its underlying system component" .


#################################################################
#    Data properties
#################################################################

###  https://www.w3id.org/fumco/has-direct-quale
<https://www.w3id.org/fumco/has-direct-quale> rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                              rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topDataProperty ;
                                              rdfs:domain <https://w3id.org/DOLCE/OWL/DOLCEbasic#Quality> ;
                                              rdfs:label "has-direct-quale" .


#################################################################
#    Classes
#################################################################

###  https://github.com/kataph/function-method-ontology#DivisionEvent
:DivisionEvent rdf:type owl:Class ;
               rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/OntologicalFunction> ;
               rdfs:label "Division Event" ;
               iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "An concept is recognized as a division event classifier if it classifies events where multiple entities appear related to some previously existing which disappears" .


###  https://github.com/kataph/function-method-ontology#EntitiyCreationEvent
:EntitiyCreationEvent rdf:type owl:Class ;
                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/OntologicalFunction> ;
                      rdfs:label "Entity Creation Event" ;
                      iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "An concept is recognized as an entity creation event classifier if it classifies events where something new appears" .


###  https://github.com/kataph/function-method-ontology#EntityDestructionEvent
:EntityDestructionEvent rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/OntologicalFunction> ;
                        rdfs:label "Entity Destruction Event" ;
                        iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "An concept is recognized as a entity destruction event classifier if it classifies events where an entity that was present before is no more" .


###  https://github.com/kataph/function-method-ontology#MereologicalJoinEvent
:MereologicalJoinEvent rdf:type owl:Class ;
                       rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/OntologicalFunction> ;
                       rdfs:label "Mereological Join Event" ;
                       iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "An concept is recognized as a mereological join event classifier if it classifies events where something new appears that has something else previously existing as part" .


###  https://github.com/kataph/function-method-ontology#ParticularOntologicalFunction
:ParticularOntologicalFunction rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/OntologicalFunction> ;
                               rdfs:comment """Adopting DOLCE as an upper ontology, ontological functions and ontological functions about particulars coincide. 

Of course, since the FUMCO ontology imports DOLCEbasic we do adopt DOLCE as an upper ontology. The reason we keep this class as a separated subclass is to help eventual users that may wish to align with different upper level ontologies: from their point of view ontological functions about particulars are DOLCE-ontological functions, which may be different than the ontological functions produced by their ontology of choice.

Note that the subclasses of this class may not be exhaustive (we skipped the DOLCE category of abstracts, judging it irrelevant for engineering functions), but those classes that refer to the (probably) most common entities referenced by engineering functions are present: (ontological function about) quality values, features, amount of matters, and physical objects. 

The additional leaf classes present (e.g. To Groove, Connect, ...) are just added to showcase how to extend the taxonomy. In particular, no claim of completeness about these is made (e.g. note that any detailed vocabulary of engineering function will contain many more verbs)""" ;
                               rdfs:label "Ontological Function about Particulars" ;
                               iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "An concept that classifies a perdurant based on what happens to any individual entity related to it" .


###  https://github.com/kataph/function-method-ontology#Reclassification
:Reclassification rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/OntologicalFunction> ;
                  rdfs:label "Reclassification" ;
                  iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "An concept is recognized as a 'reclassification' if it classifies events where some instance change its type" .


###  https://github.com/kataph/function-method-ontology#Stasis
:Stasis rdf:type owl:Class ;
        rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/fumco/OntologicalFunction> ;
        rdfs:label "Stasis" ;
        iof-av:naturalLanguageDefinition "An concept is recognized as a stasis classifier if it classifies occurrences where things do not undergo change" .


